WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.197 --> 00:00:07.238
We've all spent vacations in Italy,

00:00:08.058 --> 00:00:08.558
Venice,

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:09.320
Rome,

00:00:09.419 --> 00:00:10.060
the beaches,

00:00:10.339 --> 00:00:11.020
the churches,

00:00:11.261 --> 00:00:11.980
the food.

00:00:12.721 --> 00:00:13.301
Okay,
okay,

00:00:13.301 --> 00:00:14.742
it's a bit of a cliche to say,

00:00:15.422 --> 00:00:17.202
but across the Alps from France,

00:00:17.802 --> 00:00:19.643
it's still a magical place.

00:00:20.143 --> 00:00:21.844
I've been going there for 30 years,

00:00:22.285 --> 00:00:25.085
ever since I met a group of Italians at a vacation club.

00:00:25.506 --> 00:00:26.407
Back in those days,

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:28.448
we wore our sunglasses in our hair.

00:00:29.207 --> 00:00:34.993
We added O's and A's to every word to make ourselves understood until I decided to really learn Italian.

00:00:35.954 --> 00:00:37.375
I studied history in Verona.

00:00:38.235 --> 00:00:40.116
I worked as a bartender on Lake Garda.

00:00:40.878 --> 00:00:41.378
And finally,

00:00:41.397 --> 00:00:42.878
I worked as a sports journalist.

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:45.661
I fell in love with the country across the Alps.

00:00:46.161 --> 00:00:46.843
But nowadays,

00:00:47.122 --> 00:00:50.605
I barely recognize the Italy that I love so much.

00:00:52.106 --> 00:00:53.207
He has hypnotized,

00:00:53.429 --> 00:00:54.088
captivated,

00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:55.210
and enchanted them.

00:00:56.051 --> 00:00:58.112
The Italians have chosen their new leader,

00:00:58.454 --> 00:00:59.495
Matteo Salvini.

00:01:00.416 --> 00:01:01.757
He was elected on March 7,

00:01:01.777 --> 00:01:02.817
2018,

00:01:03.218 --> 00:01:05.781
thanks to a coalition with the Five Star Movement.

00:01:06.902 --> 00:01:09.224
Salvini has Italy at his feet.

00:01:10.246 --> 00:01:11.787
Matteo

00:01:14.269 --> 00:01:17.870
Despite the fact that there are two people who share the role of Prime Minister,

00:01:18.371 --> 00:01:21.334
Luigi Di Meo is no longer part of the official picture.

00:01:22.114 --> 00:01:23.094
In barely one year,

00:01:23.275 --> 00:01:24.075
Salvini's party,

00:01:24.215 --> 00:01:25.055
known as the League,

00:01:25.316 --> 00:01:26.596
went from 17%

00:01:26.656 --> 00:01:27.156
to 30%

00:01:27.378 --> 00:01:27.878
of votes.

00:01:27.978 --> 00:01:29.540
in the last regional elections,

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:32.463
Salvini is advancing as fast as a Ferrari.

00:01:34.305 --> 00:01:36.088
Salvini's nickname is Il Capitano,

00:01:36.328 --> 00:01:36.829
the captain.

00:01:37.168 --> 00:01:39.091
His method is to speak with no filter.

00:01:42.896 --> 00:01:44.736
of nothing and no one.

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:45.317
With this young

00:01:45.737 --> 00:01:46.599
40-something from Milan,

00:01:46.858 --> 00:01:50.501
you can forget about the polite forms of address used by the political pros.

00:01:50.742 --> 00:01:51.903
Matteo shoots from the hip.

00:01:52.444 --> 00:01:54.045
His preferred themes are migrants,

00:01:54.284 --> 00:01:55.686
the Italian political left,

00:01:55.885 --> 00:01:56.385
Europe,

00:01:56.447 --> 00:01:57.707
Merkel and even Macron.

00:01:58.048 --> 00:01:59.750
Everyone gets raked across the coals.

00:02:04.813 --> 00:02:05.313
Populist,

00:02:05.433 --> 00:02:06.855
racist and even fascist.

00:02:07.156 --> 00:02:10.557
That's how this friend of Marine Le Pen is depicted outside of Italy.

00:02:11.079 --> 00:02:11.818
In his own country,

00:02:12.139 --> 00:02:12.719
his detractor

00:02:12.979 --> 00:02:15.621
have trouble making themselves heard over the 78%

00:02:15.741 --> 00:02:18.462
of Italians who support his policy on immigration.

00:02:19.403 --> 00:02:20.044
Up until now,

00:02:20.383 --> 00:02:23.746
I'd always understood the people who had been my friends for 30 years.

00:02:24.006 --> 00:02:25.826
There were sensitive topics like Mussolini,

00:02:26.026 --> 00:02:26.546
immigration,

00:02:26.927 --> 00:02:28.187
Senadine Sedan's headbutt,

00:02:28.307 --> 00:02:29.509
but when it comes to Salvini,

00:02:29.609 --> 00:02:30.990
I find it hard to understand.

00:02:35.312 --> 00:02:41.135
I'd rather be the Minister of the Interior and send some clandestines to their homes.

00:02:41.175 --> 00:02:41.675
This is better for me.

00:02:43.576 --> 00:02:46.458
So I rented a car and went to meet some of these Italians,

00:02:46.638 --> 00:02:48.959
so they could tell me why they voted for Salvini.

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:51.941
We stopped to speak with an entrepreneur in Verona.

00:02:58.104 --> 00:02:59.305
A traditional Catholic.

00:03:02.607 --> 00:03:04.468
And then a lawyer in the La Marche region.

00:03:04.948 --> 00:03:07.929
A young student in Bologna and a metalworker.

00:03:11.570 --> 00:03:13.292
A senator who's close to Salvini.

00:03:17.372 --> 00:03:19.133
And finally,

00:03:19.293 --> 00:03:21.354
olive oil producers in the Naples region.

00:03:22.034 --> 00:03:30.318
1250 miles from north to south in Matteo Salvini's Italy,

00:03:30.818 --> 00:03:33.039
the brat who makes Europe shake in its boots.

00:03:36.675 --> 00:03:37.496
Adoptive city,

00:03:37.775 --> 00:03:38.275
Verona,

00:03:38.836 --> 00:03:40.677
the capital of the Veneto region.

00:03:42.097 --> 00:03:44.179
It has all the scenes right out of a postcard.

00:03:44.579 --> 00:03:45.280
Old stones,

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:46.359
medieval statues,

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:47.901
and elegant women in furs.

00:03:48.881 --> 00:03:49.740
Verona is rich,

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:50.681
very rich.

00:03:51.222 --> 00:03:52.682
An opulent region with 6%

00:03:53.182 --> 00:03:53.782
unemployment.

00:03:54.342 --> 00:03:55.843
It is rich with marble quarries,

00:03:55.883 --> 00:03:56.783
delicious wines,

00:03:56.804 --> 00:04:01.786
and thousands of small to medium businesses and industries which have made the Italian system successful.

00:04:02.606 --> 00:04:03.106
First stop,

00:04:03.246 --> 00:04:03.746
Busolengo,

00:04:04.127 --> 00:04:05.927
to see my old friend Luca Perabolo.

00:04:06.551 --> 00:04:09.974
He was not very enthusiastic at the idea of talking about politics.

00:04:10.574 --> 00:04:11.175
Luca is 42.

00:04:20.962 --> 00:04:24.125
He's the head sales representative for a small cosmetics company.

00:04:27.387 --> 00:04:29.108
Your colleagues from the TV also use it.

00:04:29.128 --> 00:04:29.589
Yes?

00:04:29.589 --> 00:04:30.709
Yes,
because it's opaque,

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:32.050
against the lights.

00:04:32.051 --> 00:04:32.551
Oh,
really?

00:04:32.551 --> 00:04:33.051
Yes,

00:04:34.092 --> 00:04:34.733
it's true,

00:04:34.812 --> 00:04:35.673
it's true.

00:04:35.774 --> 00:04:37.234
There are about ten employees,

00:04:37.474 --> 00:04:38.555
including Luca's wife,

00:04:38.815 --> 00:04:39.575
his brother-in-law,

00:04:39.836 --> 00:04:40.916
and his next-door neighbor.

00:04:41.317 --> 00:04:42.017
We start the interview.

00:04:57.276 --> 00:04:58.976
So they moved to the left.

00:04:58.996 --> 00:05:01.738
Years of hell for Italy,

00:05:01.838 --> 00:05:02.599
for the south,

00:05:02.600 --> 00:05:03.279
in general,

00:05:03.339 --> 00:05:04.000
for the north,

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:04.580
etc.

00:05:05.442 --> 00:05:07.022
So let's all move to the right,

00:05:07.163 --> 00:05:10.504
Berlusconi in the sense of the center-right,

00:05:10.685 --> 00:05:12.065
even the right in quotation marks.

00:05:12.085 --> 00:05:12.566
extreme,

00:05:12.566 --> 00:05:13.587
finite,

00:05:14.149 --> 00:05:20.115
to the times and even there they come out and above all there is Bossi,

00:05:20.116 --> 00:05:20.775
the old Bossi,

00:05:21.036 --> 00:05:22.678
do you remember him?

00:05:22.679 --> 00:05:24.800
I have it hard.

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:27.024
We have it hard Roma thief and then he stole more than

00:05:27.024 --> 00:05:29.346
than those in Rome.

00:05:29.425 --> 00:05:30.706
So,
who do you vote for?

00:05:31.286 --> 00:05:32.567
Who remains?

00:05:33.088 --> 00:05:33.588
I mean,

00:05:33.588 --> 00:05:36.591
there's very few left.

00:05:36.831 --> 00:05:37.411
So you vote,

00:05:37.673 --> 00:05:38.954
in my opinion,

00:05:38.954 --> 00:05:40.134
or at least I did,

00:05:40.136 --> 00:05:44.338
you vote for those who seem to have the least bad ideas.

00:05:44.398 --> 00:05:45.838
And you,

00:05:45.918 --> 00:05:48.862
what did you vote for before?

00:05:48.882 --> 00:05:52.644
So,
I did several years in which I didn't vote for anything,

00:05:52.646 --> 00:05:54.886
I cancelled the ballot.

00:05:54.887 --> 00:05:56.648
I made a big X on the whole board.

00:05:56.888 --> 00:05:58.093
Luca is a bit cynical,

00:05:58.294 --> 00:05:59.377
and yet on March 7th,

00:05:59.398 --> 00:06:00.282
2018,

00:06:00.482 --> 00:06:02.470
he casts his ballot for Salvini.

00:06:02.941 --> 00:06:03.781
I tell you the truth,

00:06:04.141 --> 00:06:15.904
not because I share my ideas or the political program of these,

00:06:16.145 --> 00:06:20.386
but to give a little attempt,

00:06:20.526 --> 00:06:23.266
a kick,

00:06:24.147 --> 00:06:27.308
an attempt to see if these,

00:06:28.088 --> 00:06:32.449
once I find one that does what he says.

00:07:11.496 --> 00:07:13.797
It was one of Salvini's campaign promises,

00:07:13.977 --> 00:07:14.717
a flat tax,

00:07:14.997 --> 00:07:17.258
a single rate income tax for individuals,

00:07:18.058 --> 00:07:19.199
but also for businesses,

00:07:19.839 --> 00:07:21.639
a rate that could be capped at 25%

00:07:21.859 --> 00:07:22.400
of revenue.

00:07:23.140 --> 00:07:25.081
Some people feel it would benefit the wealthy.

00:07:26.561 --> 00:07:27.882
Guys,

00:07:27.902 --> 00:07:30.403
it works like this everywhere.

00:07:30.404 --> 00:07:31.224
If we make money,

00:07:31.225 --> 00:07:31.705
we make them run abroad.

00:07:31.705 --> 00:07:33.405
If we make companies run abroad,

00:07:33.406 --> 00:07:35.166
if we punish those who have a nice shop,

00:07:35.286 --> 00:07:36.627
those who have a nice jacket,

00:07:36.647 --> 00:07:38.388
those who have a nice car,

00:07:38.408 --> 00:07:39.128
these go abroad,

00:07:39.129 --> 00:07:39.629
buy abroad,

00:07:39.630 --> 00:07:40.010
spend abroad,

00:07:40.010 --> 00:07:42.550
and then they work abroad.

00:07:42.551 --> 00:07:44.571
This is what convinced Luca and Stefano,

00:07:44.932 --> 00:07:47.793
who hoped that this policy would come into effect very quickly.

00:07:48.554 --> 00:07:49.134
With Salvini,

00:07:49.514 --> 00:07:51.055
it's about politics à la carte.

00:07:51.876 --> 00:07:52.576
Tailor-made,

00:07:52.936 --> 00:07:53.897
pleasing everyone.

00:07:54.337 --> 00:07:56.578
even some of the most conservative voters,

00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:01.181
building from another time in a neighborhood in Verona.

00:08:02.001 --> 00:08:04.163
We are traditional Catholic,

00:08:04.164 --> 00:08:09.125
so we are the ex-Orandi and the ex-Credendi.

00:08:09.145 --> 00:08:13.808
I'll say it in Latin so everyone can understand.

00:08:15.149 --> 00:08:17.930
Matteo Castagnà created Christus Rex,

00:08:18.231 --> 00:08:20.312
an association with roughly 50 members,

00:08:20.672 --> 00:08:22.253
including his wife and some friends.

00:08:23.085 --> 00:08:28.240
Their fight is against abortion and all those who support the practice which they consider immoral.

00:08:31.513 --> 00:08:33.795
It's a very normal practice,

00:08:33.835 --> 00:08:35.476
if you decide not to have a child,

00:08:35.477 --> 00:08:36.457
you throw it away,

00:08:36.497 --> 00:08:38.739
because it's not a life,

00:08:38.799 --> 00:08:42.343
because for them,

00:08:42.443 --> 00:08:43.404
the modern world,

00:08:43.444 --> 00:08:48.128
they decided that life happens with birth,

00:08:48.168 --> 00:08:48.868
now it's not even that,

00:08:49.129 --> 00:08:50.089
instead for us,

00:08:50.190 --> 00:08:50.750
Catholics,

00:08:50.810 --> 00:08:51.571
traditionalists,

00:08:51.572 --> 00:08:55.374
it happens when there is conception,

00:08:55.414 --> 00:08:58.657
and that's where life is born.

00:08:58.869 --> 00:09:02.771
Matteo and his wife brought their fight against abortion to the streets of Verona.

00:09:03.571 --> 00:09:04.912
They organized protests.

00:09:05.392 --> 00:09:06.112
A few months ago,

00:09:06.453 --> 00:09:07.833
faced with these religious zealots,

00:09:08.213 --> 00:09:09.694
Verona's city council gave in.

00:09:20.319 --> 00:09:37.870
of the communals of the particular way of the league of a motion that asks the municipality of who asked the municipality of verona to name verona city of life and to support associations

00:09:38.191 --> 00:09:47.257
two in particular with economic contributions which work to to discourage women from aborting.

00:09:47.981 --> 00:09:57.349
A victory that led Matteo Castagnà all the way to the Chamber of Deputies last January because Matteo and his friends from Christus found support in Salvini's government,

00:09:58.170 --> 00:10:00.892
notably in the person of Lorenzo Fontana,

00:10:01.513 --> 00:10:02.754
Minister for Family.

00:10:14.584 --> 00:10:20.647
and against abortion,

00:10:20.687 --> 00:10:23.848
obviously.

00:10:23.908 --> 00:10:25.429
And so,

00:10:30.431 --> 00:10:30.953
for us,
it was a...

00:10:30.953 --> 00:10:32.833
I don't say a miracle,

00:10:32.933 --> 00:10:35.314
but having a family minister pro-family,

00:10:35.315 --> 00:10:38.155
because until now there has never been one,

00:10:38.156 --> 00:10:38.815
is a satisfaction.

00:10:38.895 --> 00:10:41.797
The mark...

00:10:42.713 --> 00:10:47.695
He is giving to the

00:10:48.336 --> 00:10:58.220
Ministry and it seems that from a cultural point of view,

00:10:58.240 --> 00:11:01.542
he is breathing a different air in Italy.

00:11:02.322 --> 00:11:06.503
For those who believe that the good God gives us a hand,

00:11:06.883 --> 00:11:14.125
the family is founded on the union of a man.

00:11:14.185 --> 00:11:27.889
I thank His Holiness Pope Francis for repeating what is right.

00:11:28.730 --> 00:11:29.590
At least it's clear.

00:11:30.322 --> 00:11:34.105
I dare to ask one last question before leaving our friends from Christus Rex.

00:11:38.828 --> 00:11:41.050
Do you have daughters?

00:11:41.150 --> 00:11:43.692
No.
And you,

00:11:43.712 --> 00:11:46.013
ma'am?

00:11:46.053 --> 00:11:49.276
That's why we feel more and more and believe even more in the spark of life.

00:11:51.357 --> 00:11:53.339
Birth rates are a big problem in Italy.

00:11:53.739 --> 00:11:55.760
With only 1.3 babies for each woman,

00:11:56.001 --> 00:11:57.562
the country has aged a lot.

00:11:58.554 --> 00:12:01.116
Salvini promises to give it a nice facelift.

00:12:01.837 --> 00:12:03.077
To get his message across,

00:12:03.618 --> 00:12:06.180
Salvini speaks directly to his voters on social media.

00:12:06.980 --> 00:12:08.281
Berlusconi had television.

00:12:08.682 --> 00:12:09.342
With Salvini,

00:12:09.542 --> 00:12:10.183
it's Facebook.

00:12:11.744 --> 00:12:13.946
With nearly 3.5 million fans,

00:12:14.346 --> 00:12:17.948
Il Capitano is the most followed European politician on Facebook.

00:12:18.449 --> 00:12:20.370
He posts between five and six times a day.

00:12:20.691 --> 00:12:21.571
And like a good friend,

00:12:21.891 --> 00:12:23.673
Matteo puts everything on display.

00:12:24.173 --> 00:12:25.134
His passion for cats?

00:12:25.574 --> 00:12:26.455
For AC Milan,

00:12:26.755 --> 00:12:27.856
for campaign speeches,

00:12:28.176 --> 00:12:29.877
the best of his TV appearances,

00:12:30.218 --> 00:12:30.798
what he eats,

00:12:31.078 --> 00:12:33.580
and some montages that he knows the secret to.

00:12:35.642 --> 00:12:37.143
Matteo's a real geek.

00:12:38.584 --> 00:12:43.047
We're back on the road heading south towards the Adriatic coast and the region of La Marche,

00:12:44.028 --> 00:12:44.808
to Senegalia,

00:12:45.709 --> 00:12:48.411
a seaside resort between Rimini and Riccione.

00:12:50.112 --> 00:12:52.034
It's like a scene from a Fellini film.

00:12:52.538 --> 00:12:53.038
In summer,

00:12:53.379 --> 00:12:55.821
you have to fight to put your towel down on its beaches.

00:12:56.742 --> 00:12:57.183
Today,

00:12:57.183 --> 00:13:00.066
we hardly run into anyone except retirees.

00:13:01.247 --> 00:13:02.908
The young people are elsewhere.

00:13:18.054 --> 00:13:19.395
When you are caught,

00:13:19.415 --> 00:13:24.019
in both wrists,

00:13:24.079 --> 00:13:26.181
to free yourself,

00:13:26.221 --> 00:13:26.721
you open,

00:13:26.741 --> 00:13:28.923
like a shoe in your belly,

00:13:28.924 --> 00:13:32.726
then the left arm takes this arm and you turn.

00:13:32.727 --> 00:13:34.288
Here there is also a lever.

00:13:34.289 --> 00:13:40.593
He turns with me until I decide to turn him again and there is another lever,

00:13:41.173 --> 00:13:43.035
this time on the wrist,

00:13:43.075 --> 00:13:44.035
and then I find it here.

00:13:47.718 --> 00:13:49.819
This is the owner of the Jiu-Jitsu Club,

00:13:50.259 --> 00:13:51.280
Roberto Paradisi,

00:13:51.680 --> 00:13:53.161
a well-known lawyer in the region.

00:13:58.543 --> 00:13:59.264
A few months ago,

00:13:59.644 --> 00:14:07.148
Roberto had an idea to come to the aid of all those in Italy who had been victims of violence and wanted to learn how to defend themselves.

00:14:07.488 --> 00:14:11.610
He created his association with a network of martial arts clubs throughout Italy.

00:14:13.027 --> 00:14:16.388
This is a Senegal-Perugia project.

00:14:18.189 --> 00:14:18.850
In Lombardy,

00:14:19.030 --> 00:14:21.792
there are various Lombardy gyms.

00:14:22.212 --> 00:14:23.753
There are also in Milan,

00:14:24.373 --> 00:14:24.993
Rolambro,

00:14:25.053 --> 00:14:25.553
Pavia,

00:14:26.354 --> 00:14:32.418
Arese.

00:14:33.814 --> 00:14:36.976
A girl joined Milan,

00:14:37.897 --> 00:14:39.138
just recently,

00:14:39.139 --> 00:14:44.041
a girl who told us she had been robbed twice,

00:14:44.042 --> 00:14:44.861
once on the train,

00:14:46.522 --> 00:14:47.983
and she was very scared,

00:14:47.984 --> 00:14:48.664
a young girl,

00:14:48.665 --> 00:14:49.165
a girl...

00:14:53.667 --> 00:14:58.010
We have a 26-27 year old girl here.

00:14:58.070 --> 00:15:01.732
She asked us to protect her.

00:15:02.372 --> 00:15:09.937
The most difficult thing for me is to find a way to recover.

00:15:09.977 --> 00:15:16.781
I want girls to know that it is possible to get their heads up again after such a tragedy.

00:15:18.362 --> 00:15:35.732
Fighting for what is known as legitimate defense has been Paradisi's obsession ever since he defended a young Italian who was attacked in his home by his fiancé's ex-boyfriend.

00:15:43.996 --> 00:15:47.097
...and was investigated.

00:15:47.257 --> 00:15:50.679
But our order states that the criminal action is mandatory...

00:15:50.719 --> 00:15:51.919
...and that it is a legitimate defense.

00:15:52.119 --> 00:15:52.959
