of Italians under 25 voted for Salvini.

00:32:56.347 --> 00:32:59.149
Today these young people are ready to take political action.

00:32:59.930 --> 00:33:00.490
21-year-old Luca,

00:33:00.550 --> 00:33:01.171
for example,

00:33:01.211 --> 00:33:16.423
is running in May in the Pianoro Municipal Elections as a candidate for the league.

00:33:26.491 --> 00:33:31.715
It's a beautiful road,

00:33:31.716 --> 00:33:32.055
the Futa,

00:33:32.055 --> 00:33:33.676
that must be valued,

00:33:33.776 --> 00:33:36.258
so to give value to tourism.

00:33:36.259 --> 00:33:44.303
And you must be dressed in a tie or not?

00:33:44.323 --> 00:33:44.705
I will,

00:33:44.705 --> 00:33:46.545
I will also wear that,

00:33:46.546 --> 00:33:47.545
but I'm a bit like Salvini,

00:33:47.585 --> 00:33:53.069
with the fur coat and the shirt.

00:33:53.169 --> 00:33:53.850
Thank you,

00:33:53.970 --> 00:33:55.251
thank you.

00:33:57.131 --> 00:33:57.712
The next day,

00:33:57.952 --> 00:33:58.652
still in Bologna,

00:33:59.053 --> 00:34:00.734
we meet up with Umberto Lamorgia.

00:34:02.176 --> 00:34:04.158
He's the one who organized yesterday's chat,

00:34:04.518 --> 00:34:05.779
and he's rather content with it.

00:34:06.540 --> 00:34:07.781
Umberto is a smart guy.

00:34:08.381 --> 00:34:09.523
He has a master's degree.

00:34:10.003 --> 00:34:11.745
He studied marketing in France and England,

00:34:12.245 --> 00:34:13.907
but he learned politics from the league.

00:34:16.747 --> 00:34:22.691
The space and the possibility to do something concrete,

00:34:22.831 --> 00:34:24.272
even at a political level,

00:34:24.933 --> 00:34:26.654
with my ideas,

00:34:26.694 --> 00:34:29.095
which were already those.

00:34:29.096 --> 00:34:30.816
So I already had this kind of background,

00:34:30.937 --> 00:34:31.477
this idea.

00:34:31.657 --> 00:34:34.300
I also did the political training school of the League,

00:34:34.301 --> 00:34:35.402
I had followed in Milan.

00:34:35.442 --> 00:34:39.146
What is this?

00:34:39.147 --> 00:34:43.091
It is a training school organized by the League,

00:34:43.291 --> 00:34:45.814
by the League at the national level,

00:34:45.934 --> 00:34:46.615
which every time...

00:34:46.615 --> 00:34:53.681
At least one student per year organizes courses.

00:34:53.741 --> 00:34:54.741
I,
for example,

00:34:54.801 --> 00:34:56.703
was involved in a six-month weekend.

00:34:56.704 --> 00:35:02.187
So it's not a very intense commitment.

00:35:03.528 --> 00:35:07.171
The league's political training school is Matteo Salvini's creation.

00:35:08.672 --> 00:35:11.795
The debate is about training.

00:35:16.657 --> 00:35:17.157
The school,

00:35:17.217 --> 00:35:18.658
which was launched five years ago,

00:35:19.018 --> 00:35:23.020
trains and educates the League's advocates to be its political boots on the ground.

00:35:27.623 --> 00:35:29.364
The League's school is the place to be.

00:35:30.144 --> 00:35:32.365
Speakers from all backgrounds vie to be there.

00:35:32.945 --> 00:35:34.186
People like Berlusconi,

00:35:34.546 --> 00:35:35.206
economists,

00:35:35.607 --> 00:35:36.427
parliamentarians,

00:35:36.667 --> 00:35:39.469
and even star journalists from RAI Broadcasting,

00:35:39.909 --> 00:35:40.349
like Bruno...

00:35:40.349 --> 00:35:40.849
Uno Vespa,

00:35:41.050 --> 00:35:43.934
who presents the biggest political show on the public network.

00:35:44.295 --> 00:35:45.096
It's a curious mix.

00:35:58.703 --> 00:35:59.684
In this course,

00:35:59.744 --> 00:36:03.526
in this training school,

00:36:03.586 --> 00:36:06.408
we deal with macro themes every time.

00:36:06.468 --> 00:36:07.229
For example,

00:36:07.230 --> 00:36:08.029
for the first time,

00:36:08.030 --> 00:36:10.091
we deal with the history of Italy.

00:36:10.111 --> 00:36:12.132
But the history of Italy,

00:36:12.152 --> 00:36:12.953
the aspects of...

00:36:14.334 --> 00:36:28.351
come here a book crucial a critic she could she sono static on a process of unification a common I'll Italia sent a quest of orter regionalism a quest o'chiamo rechiamo a la autonomia a tifa capire

00:36:28.471 --> 00:36:30.392
the historical reasons of Italy,

00:36:30.412 --> 00:36:33.833
which had a very strong and late unity.

00:36:33.853 --> 00:36:43.876
The normal school where we all go teaches only by simplifying that the unity of Italy is the good of the world,

00:36:43.936 --> 00:36:50.258
or that European federalism would be the great perfection,

00:36:50.338 --> 00:36:51.598
etc.

00:36:51.718 --> 00:36:53.339
This is the whole school of the left.

00:36:56.763 --> 00:36:59.285
Its history filtered through the idea of the league.

00:37:00.186 --> 00:37:00.986
At the end of training,

00:37:01.126 --> 00:37:02.848
participants receive a certificate,

00:37:03.228 --> 00:37:05.730
which is indispensable if they want to join the party.

00:37:06.010 --> 00:37:06.570
And of course,

00:37:07.011 --> 00:37:08.872
their selfie with il Capitano.

00:37:10.653 --> 00:37:11.994
Behind Salvini the showman,

00:37:12.194 --> 00:37:13.656
there is a strategic thinker,

00:37:14.216 --> 00:37:15.517
who plays the provocateur,

00:37:15.937 --> 00:37:17.819
but weaves his web behind the scenes.

00:37:18.459 --> 00:37:20.881
His masterstroke was winning over the southern Italy,

00:37:21.321 --> 00:37:22.302
the Mesegiorno.

00:37:22.822 --> 00:37:23.783
The area of Italy...

00:37:23.983 --> 00:37:25.924
that he ridiculed when he was just a deputy,

00:37:26.404 --> 00:37:28.784
and the league was known as the Northern League.

00:37:30.485 --> 00:37:30.925
Salvini,

00:37:30.925 --> 00:37:31.585
the separatist,

00:37:31.685 --> 00:37:33.346
dreamed of splitting Italy in two,

00:37:33.626 --> 00:37:34.686
to create Padania,

00:37:34.966 --> 00:37:37.767
an autonomous province around the golden triangle of Milan,

00:37:37.967 --> 00:37:38.467
Turin,

00:37:38.507 --> 00:37:39.047
and Verona.

00:37:39.748 --> 00:37:40.568
Roma la drona,

00:37:40.968 --> 00:37:41.568
Rome the thief,

00:37:41.768 --> 00:37:43.789
he chanted against the capital at the time.

00:37:44.309 --> 00:37:48.310
He claimed that those in Rome lived high on the hog at the expense of northern cities.

00:37:49.390 --> 00:37:50.251
A few years later,

00:37:50.451 --> 00:37:51.531
he's changed his tune.

00:37:52.499 --> 00:37:53.319
We're headed to Rome,

00:37:53.839 --> 00:37:56.920
the capital of Italy and the seat of its political institutions.

00:38:01.462 --> 00:38:04.163
There's a soccer game this evening at Stadio Olimpico.

00:38:05.463 --> 00:38:07.944
Rome is hosting Matteo Salvini's favorite club,

00:38:08.464 --> 00:38:09.324
AC Milan.

00:38:10.085 --> 00:38:12.265
Il Capitano leaves no one indifferent here.

00:38:18.483 --> 00:38:21.767
The worst thing that could have happened in Italy.

00:38:22.187 --> 00:38:24.910
Salvini is the worst thing.

00:38:24.911 --> 00:38:27.513
He wasn't always very kind to the people of the South,

00:38:27.553 --> 00:38:29.014
though.

00:38:29.074 --> 00:38:30.075
No,
not this one.

00:38:30.115 --> 00:38:30.537
Absolutely not.

00:38:30.537 --> 00:38:31.397
We don't forget him,

00:38:31.537 --> 00:38:33.179
since we're from the South.

00:38:33.219 --> 00:38:35.922
So,
why is he so popular here in Rome?

00:38:37.635 --> 00:38:39.056
I think it's because we're all a little tired,

00:38:39.057 --> 00:38:39.436
right?

00:38:39.436 --> 00:38:41.478
Of the old political class.

00:38:41.479 --> 00:38:42.298
Of the old political class,

00:38:42.378 --> 00:38:42.819
so let's say,

00:38:42.819 --> 00:38:44.359
okay.
This is what it offers at the moment.

00:38:44.360 --> 00:38:45.700
Well,

00:38:45.720 --> 00:38:47.161
come on.
We've tried a lot.

00:38:47.181 --> 00:38:49.643
Let's try another one.

00:38:49.644 --> 00:38:52.125
I don't agree with his policies.

00:38:53.026 --> 00:38:53.606
It's a too...

00:38:55.088 --> 00:38:56.249
I don't want to say racist,

00:38:56.790 --> 00:38:59.293
but we're getting closer to racism.

00:38:59.333 --> 00:39:00.795
He says no,

00:39:00.935 --> 00:39:02.036
I'm not racist.

00:39:02.076 --> 00:39:02.777
He says no,

00:39:02.877 --> 00:39:04.239
it's normal that he says no.

00:39:04.740 --> 00:39:07.403
But what he does in reality...

00:39:08.264 --> 00:39:09.104
It shows that he is.

00:39:09.105 --> 00:39:09.745
Or at least,

00:39:09.785 --> 00:39:11.326
unfortunately,

00:39:11.346 --> 00:39:14.128
many Italians are following him.

00:39:14.129 --> 00:39:16.290
A little because there is this fear.

00:39:16.570 --> 00:39:21.454
Because he created fear in the face of the blacks,

00:39:21.455 --> 00:39:23.656
of the guys who come from outside.

00:39:23.657 --> 00:39:24.256
It's a problem,

00:39:24.357 --> 00:39:25.858
because clearly it's a problem.

00:39:25.938 --> 00:39:30.261
Because now Africa is getting in more and more every day.

00:39:30.281 --> 00:39:34.064
But we have to be more human,

00:39:34.065 --> 00:39:37.347
more humanitarian and try to help.

00:39:38.747 --> 00:39:39.388
these people.

00:39:40.008 --> 00:39:42.589
Migrants are the number one issue in Italy.

00:39:43.589 --> 00:39:45.270
Matteo Salvini's stock and trade.

00:39:46.310 --> 00:39:54.693
He built his electoral base on the fear that is provoked by this ceaseless wave of lifeboats in distress landing by the thousands on Italian shores.

00:39:54.933 --> 00:39:57.834
And the city he uses to symbolize this is Lampedusa.

00:40:02.115 --> 00:40:07.897
I prefer to be the Minister of the Interior and send some clandestine people back home.

00:40:07.898 --> 00:40:08.877
I can do this better.

00:40:09.278 --> 00:40:13.339
Salvini gave himself the mission of putting an end to the flow of immigrants once and for all.

00:40:13.699 --> 00:40:16.580
He doesn't hesitate to get angry with his European neighbors.

00:40:16.960 --> 00:40:19.941
He's a permanent guest on television shows to talk about the subject,

00:40:20.121 --> 00:40:22.062
and he proudly proclaims his track record.

00:40:25.599 --> 00:40:33.023
I will do this,

00:40:33.063 --> 00:40:35.284
these are the numbers of last year.

00:40:35.285 --> 00:40:41.707
I will deal with 2017 and 2018.

00:40:41.787 --> 00:40:44.909
Thanks to my commitment and the entire government,

00:40:44.910 --> 00:40:48.531
we have landed almost 100,000 less landings.

00:40:49.191 --> 00:40:50.093
You are privileged,

00:40:50.133 --> 00:40:51.296
you are the first to see it,

00:40:51.316 --> 00:40:51.778
probably.

00:40:51.778 --> 00:40:52.339
Here they are.

00:40:52.340 --> 00:40:55.126
The acts of the Catania Tribunal.

00:40:55.246 --> 00:40:57.973
Sections.

00:40:59.399 --> 00:41:01.420
Ministerial crimes.

00:41:01.421 --> 00:41:07.761
You already guessed that there is something that obviously concerns my person and concerns you too.

00:41:07.762 --> 00:41:08.762
Tribunal of Catania,

00:41:08.862 --> 00:41:09.362
section,

00:41:09.982 --> 00:41:12.463
ministerial crimes.

00:41:12.683 --> 00:41:15.463
I'm back to being investigated.

00:41:15.504 --> 00:41:16.364
Now I'm reading you,

00:41:16.365 --> 00:41:17.624
I'm back to being investigated.

00:41:17.864 --> 00:41:19.044
In this particular case,

00:41:19.245 --> 00:41:22.025
Salvini was saved by his parliamentary immunity.

00:41:22.665 --> 00:41:23.165
How funny.

00:41:23.866 --> 00:41:26.687
And to justify his aggressive policies against immigrants,

00:41:27.267 --> 00:41:28.527
Mateo can count on support from

00:41:29.248 --> 00:41:30.809
from an unexpected ally.

00:41:33.372 --> 00:41:34.112
Tony Iwobi,

00:41:34.413 --> 00:41:35.494
62 years old,

00:41:35.814 --> 00:41:37.035
originally from Nigeria,

00:41:37.295 --> 00:41:51.990
made history last year.

00:41:54.331 --> 00:41:56.012
He arrived in Italy as a bricklayer.

00:41:56.192 --> 00:41:57.993
In 1996,

00:41:58.294 --> 00:42:03.217
Tony Iwobi became a member of the League and an active campaigner in the Bergamo region.

00:42:03.937 --> 00:42:06.359
The senator has known Salvini for a long time,

00:42:06.799 --> 00:42:07.299
so in

00:42:07.880 --> 00:42:09.281
2014, Matteo came to Italy.

00:42:24.239 --> 00:42:28.541
I have a very good relationship with my troops.

00:42:28.981 --> 00:42:30.342
You said immediately yes,

00:42:30.382 --> 00:42:31.522
I will do it without any hesitation.

00:42:31.523 --> 00:42:36.684
Why am I the only African representative to choose immigration?

00:42:36.685 --> 00:42:38.285
Is there a risk or no?

00:42:38.565 --> 00:42:39.186
Absolutely,

00:42:39.226 --> 00:42:44.608
because I saw it as a call for responsibility.

00:42:45.348 --> 00:42:50.971
Because I felt that someone had to make them understand what immigration is.

00:42:52.055 --> 00:42:52.616
Look,
the League,

00:42:52.616 --> 00:42:54.016
I say it with all my heart,

00:42:54.017 --> 00:42:56.257
without any middle ground,

00:42:56.557 --> 00:42:57.177
the League,

00:42:57.817 --> 00:42:59.658
at least the League of Matteo Salvini,

00:43:00.438 --> 00:43:04.340
has never been against immigration as such.

00:43:04.380 --> 00:43:07.001
Because we are aware,

00:43:07.041 --> 00:43:09.061
he himself told me,

00:43:09.062 --> 00:43:10.522
he has always told me,

00:43:10.542 --> 00:43:12.523
that no one...

00:43:13.423 --> 00:43:15.165
on the face of the earth,

00:43:15.705 --> 00:43:16.486
on this planet,

00:43:16.766 --> 00:43:18.367
can stop immigration.

00:43:19.208 --> 00:43:21.310
Because immigration belongs to man.

00:43:21.390 --> 00:43:23.231
Immigration is in the DNA of man.

00:43:23.271 --> 00:43:26.213
But it must be regulated.

00:43:26.214 --> 00:43:30.257
And it is the task of the policy to regulate it.

00:43:30.457 --> 00:43:33.640
What has happened in this country in the last seven years,

00:43:33.641 --> 00:43:36.662
in the countries of the left government?

00:43:38.079 --> 00:43:42.322
It has nothing to do with the immigration I know or experienced.

00:43:42.402 --> 00:43:50.808
I am also fighting for my fellow Continentals who will understand sooner or later.

00:43:50.888 --> 00:43:56.773
Because by facilitating uncontrolled immigration,

00:43:57.333 --> 00:43:58.314
clandestinity,

00:43:59.815 --> 00:44:03.538
it is the greatest idiocy and crime that man can commit.

00:44:05.819 --> 00:44:06.679
I know what you're thinking.

00:44:07.260 --> 00:44:11.122
Tony is Salvini's decoy to justify his policy on immigration.

00:44:11.682 --> 00:44:12.182
Maybe.

00:44:12.783 --> 00:44:13.383
In any case,

00:44:13.643 --> 00:44:16.105
the senator takes his role very seriously.

00:44:26.911 --> 00:44:30.393
to be able to concentrate on the territory to solve these problems,

00:44:30.413 --> 00:44:36.357
because they had really created an unacceptable situation.

00:44:36.358 --> 00:44:37.458
Even for us Africans,

00:44:37.459 --> 00:44:39.379
we were ashamed,

00:44:39.419 --> 00:44:41.641
seeing our fellow nationals,

00:44:41.801 --> 00:44:42.882
human beings,

00:44:42.883 --> 00:44:44.003
who were abandoned,

00:44:44.103 --> 00:44:45.463
to their fate,

00:44:46.084 --> 00:44:47.165
on the territory.

00:44:48.265 --> 00:44:49.126
To end the interview,

00:44:49.206 --> 00:44:55.510
we talked about soccer and the hateful messages of certain Italians toward the French team during the World Cup.

00:44:56.715 --> 00:44:57.515
For the first time,

00:44:57.595 --> 00:44:59.336
an African team has won the World Cup.

00:45:02.777 --> 00:45:03.537
But once again,

00:45:03.957 --> 00:45:06.038
Tony Iwobi evaded the question.

00:45:14.560 --> 00:45:15.861
But there's nothing to laugh about.

00:45:17.041 --> 00:45:17.541
True,

00:45:17.561 --> 00:45:20.562
Salvini blocked the flow of migrants who were landing in Italy.

00:45:22.163 --> 00:45:23.323
But they moved on to Spain.

00:45:25.027 --> 00:45:25.947
not to mention those who,

00:45:26.347 --> 00:45:27.028
stuck in Libya,

00:45:27.208 --> 00:45:27.988
were enslaved.

00:45:33.970 --> 00:45:34.630
Far from there,

00:45:35.310 --> 00:45:35.971
from now on,

00:45:36.511 --> 00:45:37.911
the Italians sleep peacefully.

00:45:38.971 --> 00:45:43.313
But the man who dreams of being the only prime minister has another step to take,

00:45:44.053 --> 00:45:45.213
no doubt the most difficult,

00:45:45.634 --> 00:45:47.334
reconciling with the people of Naples,

00:45:47.734 --> 00:45:49.695
with whom he has a bone of contention.

00:46:09.627 --> 00:46:11.628
He claims it was a youthful indiscretion,

00:46:11.908 --> 00:46:12.748
a different time,

00:46:13.048 --> 00:46:15.950
when he was a hot-headed campaigner for the Northern League.

00:46:19.671 --> 00:46:22.512
Naples and Salerno region are the Garden of Italy,

00:46:23.252 --> 00:46:27.534
with its agricultural plains and its thousands of greenhouses like mirrors.

00:46:28.715 --> 00:46:30.635
The region's other bounty is olive oil,

00:46:31.476 --> 00:46:33.317
made with the Rotondella variety.

00:46:34.077 --> 00:46:36.718
It's less well-known than olive oil from Puglia,

00:46:37.618 --> 00:46:39.259
and has a very particular taste.

00:46:42.037 --> 00:46:44.299
This is sweeter.

00:46:44.379 --> 00:46:44.999
This one is sweeter.

00:46:45.000 --> 00:46:49.423
Because those who use it everywhere prefer a less aggressive taste.

00:46:49.424 --> 00:46:51.505
I prefer the other one.

00:46:51.506 --> 00:46:52.086
Yes,
me too.

00:46:54.287 --> 00:47:00.313
The Di Giorgio brothers took over the family business years ago and are grooming their children to take over from them.

00:47:01.154 --> 00:47:01.654
However,

00:47:01.774 --> 00:47:03.556
the industry is not flourishing.

00:47:08.448 --> 00:47:12.111
You used to do this with your hands?

00:47:12.331 --> 00:47:13.311
Yes,

00:47:13.331 --> 00:47:15.733
once you used to pick up...

00:47:15.753 --> 00:47:16.834
Did you do it?

00:47:16.835 --> 00:47:17.376
No,
I didn't.

00:47:17.376 --> 00:47:17.876
I remember.

00:47:18.015 --> 00:47:21.017
Young people don't want to make sacrifices in the countryside.

00:47:21.018 --> 00:47:22.579
In the countryside,

00:47:22.580 --> 00:47:23.539
they all run away.

00:47:24.260 --> 00:47:25.020
Why don't you pay?

00:47:25.081 --> 00:47:26.281
Not because I don't pay,

00:47:26.301 --> 00:47:28.283
because at work...

00:47:29.684 --> 00:47:32.126
It's very stressful.

00:47:32.127 --> 00:47:34.328
And so many sacrifices are required.

00:47:34.408 --> 00:47:37.371
And then you don't get the work you put in.

00:47:37.451 --> 00:47:40.113
Because there is a lot of competition from outside.

00:47:40.394 --> 00:47:40.794
For example,

00:47:40.794 --> 00:47:41.195
in Italy,

00:47:41.195 --> 00:47:43.957
if you want to make a liter of good oil here in our area,

00:47:44.397 --> 00:47:46.219
you have to sell it for at least 6-7 euros.

00:47:47.259 --> 00:47:48.220
But to get the expenses,

00:47:48.221 --> 00:47:49.602
it's not that you earn it.

00:47:49.603 --> 00:47:54.546
And then you go to the supermarket and they sell it for 3-4 euros.

00:47:54.586 --> 00:47:55.847
It's all imported oil.

00:47:56.031 --> 00:47:57.452
And he can't sell it for 6 or 7 euros.

00:47:57.453 --> 00:48:02.233
And he can't recover how much he spent.

00:48:03.053 --> 00:48:05.894
Faced with the anguish of these Neapolitan producers,

00:48:06.395 --> 00:48:08.395
Salvini has perhaps found a solution.

00:48:08.495 --> 00:48:11.236
Making a profit is a political act.

00:48:11.237 --> 00:48:16.058
Because it is clear that the same milk that is paid 60 cents in Sardinia and in Italy,

00:48:17.078 --> 00:48:19.299
in Romania is paid less than half.

00:48:20.155 --> 00:48:21.516
30 cents,

00:48:21.736 --> 00:48:26.820
so buying Italian means being well and helping Italian workers.

00:48:27.160 --> 00:48:28.901
Salvini is doing the battle,

00:48:28.902 --> 00:48:31.323
but in Honord it is true,

00:48:31.324 --> 00:48:34.685
it was a battle that had already started for a few decades,

00:48:34.705 --> 00:48:35.586
in short,

00:48:35.606 --> 00:48:38.968
on the protection of national productions.

00:48:39.488 --> 00:48:46.573
The point is that we have managed to have the standards that establish the traceability,

00:48:46.733 --> 00:48:47.274
the label,

00:48:47.334 --> 00:48:48.735
the origin of the raw material.

00:48:49.287 --> 00:48:50.767
But there is still a lack of control.

00:48:52.368 --> 00:48:55.389
National food preferences interest the Di Giorgio brothers.

00:48:56.689 --> 00:48:59.890
Domenico deals with agricultural issues in the region for the league.

00:49:00.931 --> 00:49:03.771
He used to vote for Forza Italia and Berlusconi,

00:49:04.552 --> 00:49:06.512
but despite Salvini's taunting words,

00:49:06.932 --> 00:49:08.593
he won them over with his actions.

00:49:09.593 --> 00:49:13.214
I think the battles he is waging are already visible.

00:49:13.274 --> 00:49:15.435
On immigration it is evident that...

00:49:15.823 --> 00:49:20.125
...that managed to block a migratory flow that invaded Italy every year.

00:49:20.205 --> 00:49:21.526
Today it is a reality.

00:49:21.527 --> 00:49:21.846
Now,

00:49:21.846 --> 00:49:24.688
the method that it is using will be debatable,

00:49:24.748 --> 00:49:26.249
but the result has been achieved.

00:49:26.309 --> 00:49:28.190
Undoubtedly.

00:49:28.210 --> 00:49:29.450
Legitimate defense,

00:49:29.451 --> 00:49:31.391
which will now become law,

00:49:31.452 --> 00:49:34.913
is another topic that is at the heart of the Italians.

00:49:34.914 --> 00:49:39.656
It is unimaginable that one cannot stay at home at ease.

00:49:41.117 --> 00:49:43.538
Salvini's doctrine has been learned by heart,

00:49:43.958 --> 00:49:44.999
even in southern Italy.

00:49:45.931 --> 00:49:46.671
Last February,

00:49:46.812 --> 00:49:49.033
during Sardinia's regional elections,

00:49:49.373 --> 00:49:51.694
the league's candidate received 48%

00:49:51.695 --> 00:49:52.195
of votes.

00:49:53.515 --> 00:49:56.257
The five-star movement got only 11%.

00:49:57.358 --> 00:49:59.039
All of this in barely a year.

00:49:59.859 --> 00:50:00.379
Impressive.

00:50:01.180 --> 00:50:05.022
The Salvini phenomenon and his success resonate outside of Italy.

00:50:08.164 --> 00:50:13.767
This was last November.

00:50:14.339 --> 00:50:15.200
The young man there,

00:50:15.380 --> 00:50:18.122
reading from his sheets of paper in halting Italian,

00:50:18.542 --> 00:50:19.703
is Jordan Bardella,

00:50:20.343 --> 00:50:22.405
who leads the list for the national rally.

00:50:23.045 --> 00:50:25.046
He was invited to speak by the youth league,

00:50:25.427 --> 00:50:28.309
and Jordan Bardella needed no urging to take the stage,

00:50:28.689 --> 00:50:29.489
because nowadays,

00:50:29.830 --> 00:50:32.051
for all its populist political parties in Europe,

00:50:32.471 --> 00:50:34.433
the league is the example to follow.

00:50:44.311 --> 00:50:48.273
Demonstrate che stoppare l'immigrazione è possibile.

00:50:49.734 --> 00:50:53.916
Demostrate che riportare la sicurezza in Italia è possibile.

00:50:54.777 --> 00:50:55.777
Nelle vostre vie,

00:50:56.438 --> 00:50:58.719
nelle vostre campagne e sulle vostre...

00:51:23.295 --> 00:51:31.901
One of the goals of Salvini is to have this kind of big coalition in Europe of all the sovereignist parties that are attached to what Salvini calls the revolution of common sense,

00:51:31.902 --> 00:51:38.145
those who want to defend the identity of European peoples and those who want to give back trust to the people in the people's place.

00:51:38.605 --> 00:51:39.145
The success of

00:51:39.606 --> 00:51:40.526
Salvini gives you wings,

00:51:40.527 --> 00:51:41.186
gives you hope?

00:51:41.946 --> 00:51:44.107
Salvini is the example that it is possible.

00:51:44.227 --> 00:51:49.229
It is the example that when you want,

00:51:49.309 --> 00:51:50.129
you can.

00:51:50.309 --> 00:51:56.631
It is the example that when you want to give the power back to the people,

00:51:56.651 --> 00:51:58.152
then it is possible.

00:51:58.192 --> 00:52:05.454
And it is the example that if the people want to take power again,

00:52:05.555 --> 00:52:06.475
then they can.

00:52:08.779 --> 00:52:09.279
Luca,

00:52:09.840 --> 00:52:11.321
Matteo Castagna and his wife,

00:52:11.661 --> 00:52:12.502
Mr.
Paradisi,

00:52:12.742 --> 00:52:13.783
the mayor of Santa Gata,

00:52:14.043 --> 00:52:14.543
Niccolò,

00:52:14.723 --> 00:52:15.244
Maurizio,

00:52:15.684 --> 00:52:16.505
Senator Uobi,

00:52:17.025 --> 00:52:18.406
and the DiGiorgio brothers,

00:52:18.967 --> 00:52:22.589
they all have a good reason to have voted for and supported Matteo Salvini.

00:52:23.630 --> 00:52:26.392
But the prime minister's outrageousness will have consequences.

00:52:26.712 --> 00:52:28.614
There's a split within Italian society,

00:52:28.914 --> 00:52:30.815
the different sides are becoming more agitated,

00:52:31.036 --> 00:52:32.336
and the worst is never far off.

00:52:32.657 --> 00:52:33.197
For example,

00:52:33.217 --> 00:52:34.078
what happened on March 21st,

00:52:34.079 --> 00:52:35.599
2019.

00:52:39.599 --> 00:52:42.520
A bus created chaos on a highway in the suburbs of Milan.

00:52:42.860 --> 00:52:46.442
These school children you see screaming and running are coming back from hell.

00:52:48.683 --> 00:52:49.403
At 11 a.m.,

00:52:49.463 --> 00:52:50.203
their bus driver,

00:52:50.664 --> 00:52:51.164
Usenio,

00:52:51.724 --> 00:52:53.505
an Italian of Senegalese origin,

00:52:53.965 --> 00:52:55.425
tied them up along with their teachers,

00:52:55.846 --> 00:52:56.986
doused the bus with gas,

00:52:57.406 --> 00:52:58.807
and threatened to burn them alive.

00:52:59.567 --> 00:53:04.232
The police arrived just in time and saved 51 students before the bus caught fire.

00:53:04.613 --> 00:53:05.514
With his crazy act,

00:53:05.754 --> 00:53:09.538
the bus driver wanted to protest the deaths of migrants in the Mediterranean.

00:53:09.859 --> 00:53:11.581
He holds Salvini responsible,

00:53:12.061 --> 00:53:14.764
an accusation which obviously doesn't hold up.

00:53:15.465 --> 00:53:20.010
But it's a sign that something is amiss in Salvolini land.

